From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: wcss-sec: do not wait for a coredump reader

An inline coredump makes recovery wait until userspace reads the dump,
or until the devcoredump timeout of five minutes runs out. With no
reader, the WCSS stays stopped that long after every firmware crash,
and Wi-Fi with it. Default to no coredump; it can still be enabled
through the remoteproc coredump sysfs attribute.

On an IPQ8074, a simulated firmware assert under a 900 Mbit/s Wi-Fi
downlink now recovers both radios in 1.2 s and the stations stay
associated; with the inline dump the WCSS was not restarted within 54 s.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec.c
@@ -364,7 +364,7 @@ static int wcss_sec_probe(struct platfor
 	qcom_add_ssr_subdev(rproc, &wcss->ssr_subdev, desc->ss_name);
 
 	rproc->auto_boot = false;
-	rproc->dump_conf = RPROC_COREDUMP_INLINE;
+	rproc->dump_conf = RPROC_COREDUMP_DISABLED;
 	rproc_coredump_set_elf_info(rproc, ELFCLASS32, EM_NONE);
 
 	if (desc->use_tmelcom) {
